    "updated_at": "2026-11-23T18:50:25Z",
    "body": "Port to the current frame. New head `1962fd5dc`.\n\n- The branch merges the ported #2964 head `4a94c23ce`. It does not use the old setup writer of this branch. The SBL comes from `agie_setup.rs` (zero erosion steps, `ID_PUNCH c_punch`, 1.0 mm separation).\n- Conflicts:\n  - `agie_profile.rs`: the contour now comes from `closed_vertical_prism`. The convex prism refusal is removed. The refusal texts use the new names of #3537.\n  - `agie/contour.rs`: the convex refusal of #2955 is replaced by the reentrant reach check. The stock, miter and setup checks of #2964 and #2984 stay. The reach and the spacing use the rough offset of the selected thickness from `QN2_OFFSETS_UM`.\n  - `agie/tests.rs`, `tests/agie_native.rs` and the user guide: both sides are kept.\n- The spacing check moved to `agie/spacing.rs`. The reentrant tests moved to `agie/reentrant_tests.rs` and `tests/agie_native/reentrant.rs`. Each file stays under 400 lines.\n- New tests pin the reach at each measured thickness and the zero-step SBL of the notched job.\n- The gate result is in the PR body. The one red step is the known gpu clippy finding.\n- The ported job was not imported on the offline control. Import `NOTCH20` on the control VM before machine use.\n",
    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
